  data: {
    LLM: "For Beginners\n1. Start as a Seen Player: Look at your cards to understand hand values\n2. Play Strong Hands Aggressively: Bet and raise with trails, pure sequences\n3. Fold Weak Hands: Don't chase with high card only\n4. Learn Hand Rankings: Memorize the order of hands\n5. Manage Your Bankroll: Don't bet more than you can afford to lose\n\nBlind Play Strategy\nAdvantages: Lower betting requirements, psychological pressure on seen players\nWhen to Play Blind: Early in the game, with small stakes, or to confuse opponents\nWhen to Look: When stakes get high or when considering a sideshow\n\nBluffing Techniques\nSemi-Bluff: Bet aggressively with drawing hands (potential sequences)\nPure Bluff: Represent strong hands with weak cards\nTiming: Bluff when opponents show weakness\nTable Image: Establish a tight image to make bluffs more credible",
